Hi Ruby,

>From your code, I can see that you provided 3 different initial values but when you passed them inside your “Build model”, you were using only the first block of initial values i.e., init.vals[[1]] for all the 3 chains and setting a seed will produce the same results irrespective of the number of chains.

I think you should either pass it through parallelization or just use for loop with init.vals[[i]].

The nimble user manual will be your good resource.
Let me know if this helps.

Thanks,
Kenny

