hi Brennan,

Thanks - I was reading too quickly yesterday eve, hence my misguided response regarding the data not being provided.

I'm able to reproduce the problem. It's a seg fault, likely a problem writing to an invalid memory location. These can be stochastic
so it's not too surprising that Heather was able to run without an issue.

One clue is that I see this warning: `warning: logProb of data node y[1, 1:2]: logProb is -Inf.` So there does seem to be some issue
with the values in the model at some point. At the same time, the model is straightforward so it's surprising that nimble would have a
seg fault with this.

